@page "/account-deletion"
@inherits AccountDeletionModel

<PageTitle>Account Deletion - Streamtunes</PageTitle>

<div class="container my-5">
    <h1 class="mb-4">Account Deletion</h1>

    <p class="text-muted"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> April 24, 2026</p>

    <p>
        This page explains how to delete your Streamtunes account, what must happen before deletion,
        and what information is removed when your request is completed.
    </p>

    <section class="mb-4">
        <h2>How to Delete Your Account</h2>
        <ol>
            <li>In the Android app, open <strong>Account Settings</strong> and choose <strong>Delete My Account</strong>.</li>
            <li>On the website, sign in and open <a href="/manage-account">Manage Account</a>, then choose <strong>Delete Account</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>You must complete the confirmation prompt before the deletion request is accepted.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-4">
        <h2>Before You Delete</h2>

        <h3>Cancel Any Active Subscription</h3>
        <p>
            You must cancel any active subscription before deleting your account. Once the subscription has been
            cancelled, you can proceed with account deletion. Deleting your account ends access tied to that account
            and removes your playlists and account data.
        </p>

        <h3>Active Creators Must Stop First</h3>
        <p>
            If you are currently an active creator, you must first open
            <a href="/CreatorSettings">Creator / Artist Settings</a> and use
            <strong>Stop Being a Creator</strong> before deleting your account.
        </p>
        <p>
            Stopping being a creator removes your uploaded songs from Streamtunes, deletes the associated song files
            from storage, and removes those songs from playlists across the service. After that step is complete,
            you can delete your user account.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-4">
        <h2>What We Delete</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Your account profile and sign-in data, including your email login and passkeys</li>
            <li>Your playlists and playlist memberships</li>
            <li>Your likes, dislikes, and song reports</li>
            <li>Your mobile verification codes and similar account-access records</li>
            <li>Your subscription records and related account associations</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Streamtunes currently works through subscription access. If you create a new account later,
            your deleted playlists and settings will not be restored.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-4">
        <h2>What May Be Retained</h2>
        <p>
            We may retain limited records when required for security, fraud prevention, legal compliance,
            tax and accounting obligations, or backup recovery windows.
        </p>
        <p>
            Some historical stream or payout records may remain only in de-identified or disassociated form
            after account deletion.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-4">
        <h2>Create a New Account Later</h2>
        <p>
            You can register for a new Streamtunes account in the future, but account deletion is permanent for the
            deleted profile. Your previous playlists, preferences, and other deleted account data will not come back
            automatically.
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
